2026-11-06T02:57:03.2772824Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T02:57:03.2773474Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T02:57:03.2774248Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T02:57:03.2774617Z 
2026-11-06T02:57:03.2774938Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T02:57:03.2775388Z 
2026-11-06T02:57:03.2775763Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T02:57:03.2776529Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T02:57:03.2776978Z 
2026-11-06T02:57:03.2777195Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T02:57:03.2777717Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T02:57:03.2778021Z 
2026-11-06T02:57:03.2778274Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T02:57:03.2778679Z   $ sh ./install-nix
